;; Math (owner L12): the names of java.lang.Math that Clojure code writes (stdlib §4.10, §4.16; only
;; Math/abs is tranche 1, the rest of the module is tranche 4). It is `:require`d with its own name,
;; (:require [Math :as Math]), and used as (Math/abs x); the Java class names become implicit aliases
;; only with E15. Not under fib.*: it is a Java name, so after the flip it takes no implicit :use
;; (plan §4.1) and the one it needs is written here.
;;
;; Decided here: abs is written out in this module. Row Math/abs says "as abs", and abs is
;; fib.core.num's, package L1's; that part was still a stub when this was written, and a cross-package
;; wait with no `open:` label to carry it is worse than one function twice. When L1's abs has landed
;; the body below becomes (fib.core/abs x) and the three comparisons go (the cases do not change).
;; It is the same function: generic over Num, Ord and Unit, so every width and both float widths
;; work; it traps on the minimum of an integer type (the neg overflows: `integer overflow in neg at
;; i64`, where Java's Math.abs returns the minimum); and it gives 0.0 for -0.0 and NaN for NaN, as Java
;; does, which a bare (if (< x 0) (neg x) x) does not for the first (case 654).
(ns Math (:use fib.core))

(defun abs (x: t) :where ((Num t) (Ord t) (Unit t)) -> t
  (let ((z (zero x)))
    (if (< x z) (neg x) (if (= x z) z x))))
